{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nqueues=[('event_alignment',179,[{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','stress_aligned','--model','research_model','--days','3','--ends','2026-09-13','2026-09-19','2026-10-05','--workers','4','--config','{\\\"seasonal\\\":true,\\\"events\\\":true,\\\"event_bar_alignment\\\":true}'],'log':'agent/results/stress_aligned_suite.log'}]),('baseline_full',178,[{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','baseline_full','--model','baseline','--days','10','--ends','2026-09-19','2026-10-11','--workers','4'],'log':'agent/results/baseline_full_suite.log'}])]\nfor name,pid,jobs in queues:\n path=Path(f'agent/queue_{name}.json');path.write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\n with open(f'agent/results/queue_{name}.log','w') as log:\n  p=subprocess.Popen(['uv','run','agent/queue_research.py','--after-pid',str(pid),'--jobs',str(path)],stdout=log,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,start_new_session=True)\n print(name,p.pid,'after',pid)\nPY\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nResource scheduling: on this resumed process tree, bounded queues reserve the cores of existing suites instead of oversubscribing. After clock exits: residual proxy fit, fine-event diagnostics/fit, then Sobol suite (2 cores). After stress_events exits: aligned-event suite (4 cores). After stress_seasonal exits: seeded starter baseline on TWO TEN-DAY windows, scored Sep09–18 and Oct01–10 inclusive (4 cores). Current weekly and stress_mixture retain 2 cores each. Maximum remains 14. New baseline_full establishes the final longer-window comparison; it does not use ranks or post-cutoff data. Queues are scripts, not agents; no subagent delegation.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
