{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/run_suite.py');s=p.read_text().replace('import argparse, subprocess, os','import argparse, subprocess, os, json\\\\nimport pyarrow.parquet as pq')\ns=s.replace(\\\"if prefix.with_suffix('.json').exists() and prefix.with_suffix('.parquet').exists():return\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"if prefix.with_suffix('.json').exists() and prefix.with_suffix('.parquet').exists():\n  try:\n   summary=json.loads(prefix.with_suffix('.json').read_text())\n   if summary['num_prompts']>0 and pq.ParquetFile(prefix.with_suffix('.parquet')).metadata.num_rows>0:return\n  except (ValueError,OSError,KeyError):pass\\\"\\\"\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nEvaluation durability: write candidate parquet and summary via temporary files and atomic renames, with summary published last. The suite resumes only when a valid JSON summary and readable nonempty parquet footer both exist, preventing an interrupted write from being mistaken for a completed cell. This changes storage only; official scoring is unchanged. Historical experiment arrays are float64 NumPy files (as were the starter JSON floats); the harness's canonical generator writes float32. Before final nomination, repeat the selected model and baseline at canonical float32 precision to bound any effect on small sampling gains.\nEOF\ncat agent/BUDGET.md && tail -4 agent/results/chronos_suite.log && wc -l agent/results/baseline_full_suite.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
