{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > agent/diagnose_dependence.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Return-dependence diagnostics only; all CRPS remains official.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import default_store_root\nassets=['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500'];out={}\nfor asset in assets:\n fs=[f for f in sorted(default_store_root(asset).glob('date=*.parquet')) if '2026-06-01'<=f.stem[5:]<'2026-09-01']\n d=pd.concat([pd.read_parquet(f,columns=['timestamp','close']) for f in fs]).set_index('timestamp').sort_index()\n price=np.log(d.close.astype(float));r={lag:price.diff(lag) for lag in [1,5,30,60]}\n moments={lag:float(x.pow(2).mean()/lag) for lag,x in r.items()}\n values={'rho1':float(r[1].corr(r[1].shift(1))),'rho5':float(r[5].corr(r[5].shift(5))),\n         'vol5_over1':float(np.sqrt(moments[5]/moments[1])),\n         'vol30_over5':float(np.sqrt(moments[30]/moments[5])),\n         'vol60_over1':float(np.sqrt(moments[60]/moments[1]))}\n out[asset]=values;print(asset,{k:round(v,4) for k,v in values.items()},flush=True)\nPath('agent/results/dependence_diagnostics.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2))\nPY\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration 16 — dependence between successive returns (prepared)\n\nHypothesis: stochastic volatility changes marginal widths but independent increments still impose square-root-of-time aggregation. Bid/ask bounce or short-lived price reversals can make minute volatility overstate longer-horizon uncertainty, especially on perpetual venues. Measure adjacent-return correlations and variance aggregation ratios on June–August data before implementing anything. If effects are material, test a strongly shrunk, context-estimated AR(1) return dependence while preserving each base-step variance. This uses only one asset's observed context and drops missing pairs.\n\nKill criterion: skip simulation work if correlations and aggregation ratios are negligible; otherwise require official CRPS improvement across multiple windows. Do not infer predictive drift from a variance-ratio diagnostic.\nEOF\ncat agent/BUDGET.md && tail -3 agent/results/chronos_suite.log && wc -l agent/results/candidate_v1_full_suite.log agent/results/candidate_v2_full_suite.log agent/results/stratified_suite.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
