{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_122","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'fast_half|config=|config =|def simulate|initial=' agent/modeling.py; cat agent/results/empirical_suite.log; tail -3 agent/results/chronos_fast15_suite.log; cat agent/suggestions.md; cat agent/paired.py\"","aggregated_output":"105:def simulate(asset,start_time,time_increment=300,time_length=86400,num_simulations=1000,context_prices=None):\n108:    config={'seasonal':True,'clock':True,'events':True,\n115:def simulate_config(asset,start_time,time_increment,time_length,num_simulations,context_prices,rng,c):\n142:        initial=long=float(np.mean(rv))\n146:            initial=.6*estimate(c.get('fast_half',60))+.25*estimate(360)+.15*long\n148:            initial=.5*estimate(c.get('fast_half',720))+.5*long\nagent/results/empirical/BTC_24h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/empirical/ETH_24h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/empirical/BTC_1h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/chronos_fast15/BTC_1h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/chronos_fast15/ETH_1h_2026-09-16 0\n# Suggestions for the benchmark and future work\n\n- The campaign says BUDGET.md is at the workspace root; this run's harness writes agent/BUDGET.md. Align the documented location.\n- Keep the raw-context issuance cutoff explicit. The supplied evaluator originally took the last 10080 rows before issuance; the official generator uses the seven calendar days ending at issuance. This run aligns with the official generator.\n- Daily NumPy predictions substantially reduce serialization overhead compared with one JSON file per prompt. The official loader already supports them; make this the default in the starter evaluator.\n- Calendar data sometimes co-locates GDP and PCE. Treat their effects jointly instead of estimating independent additive effects from the same release observations.\n- DATA.md omits the measured scored-prompt span described in CAMPAIGN.md. This bundle starts on September 8, 2026 at approximately 23:00 UTC, despite