{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_162","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration24 — uncertainty that changes within a path\n\nHypothesis: the selected mixture gives each path one constant latent volatility for its whole horizon. A stationary mean-reverting log-volatility process can preserve every base-step mixture marginal while allowing uncertainty to change over time. Replace the constant latent normal with an AR(1) Gaussian state, half-life one quarter of the forecast horizon (15min for1h,6h for24h), same stationary std0.35 and unit expected variance multiplier. Preserve the original initial latent draw and innovation draws for a closer comparison. No return drift or cross-asset inputs are introduced.\n\nTest against mixture0.35 at1000 paths on initial windows for COM and crypto1h. Kill criterion: improve both configuration/window means and most asset cells before stress/combination. The empirical innovation experiment already illustrates that more within-path variation can harm one-hour volatility CRPS; report that tradeoff rather than assuming stochastic volatility must win. Queue behind empirical_mix's two workers.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text();needle='        z*=np.exp(mix*mixture_normal-mix*mix)';assert s.count(needle)==1;s=s.replace(needle,'''        if c.get('mix_revert',False):\n            from scipy.signal import lfilter\n            half_seconds=time_length*c.get('mix_half_fraction',.25)\n            rho=2**(-time_increment/half_seconds)\n            shocks=rng.normal(size=(n,steps))*np.sqrt(1-rho*rho)\n            shocks[:,0]=mixture_normal[:,0]\n            mixture_normal=lfilter([1.],[1.,-rho],shocks,axis=1)\n        z*=np.exp(mix*mixture_normal-mix*mix)''');p.write_text(s)\njobs=[{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','mixture_reversion','--model','research_model','--config',json.dumps({'seasonal':True,'mix':.35,'mix_scope':'non_crypto24h','mix_revert':True}),'--skip-crypto24h','--workers','2'],'log':'agent/results/mixture_reversion_suite.log'}]\nPath('agent/queue_mixture_reversion.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_mixture_reversion.json --after-pid 20025 > agent/results/queue_mixture_reversion.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_163","type":"agent_message","text":"Empirical innovations are less effective than the selected volatility mixture for one-hour forecasts, and combining them has worsened every completed one-hour comparison. I’ll next test the mixture’s time dependence: keep its marginal distribution unchanged, but let latent volatility evolve within each path instead of staying fixed for the whole horizon.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_164","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.signal import lfilter\nrng=np.random.default_rng(20261011)\nfor step,horizon in [(60,3600),(300,86400)]:\n rho=2**(-step/(horizon*.25));v=np.array([1.]);means=[]\n # Exact variance recursion for the stationary latent process; no market-score substitute.\n for _ in range(horizon//step-1):v=np.append(v,rho*rho*v[-1]+1-rho*rho)\n assert np.max(np.abs(v-1))<1e-12\n n=20000;k=min(horizon//step,30);initial=rng.normal(size=n)\n eps=rng.normal(size=(n,k))*np.sqrt(1-rho*rho);eps[:,0]=initial\n state=lfilter([1],[1,-rho],eps,axis=1)\n print('horizon',horizon,'exact variance error',np.max(abs(v-1)),'sample latent variance',state.var(),'initial preservation',np.array_equal(state[:,0],initial))\nPY\nuv run agent/summarize.py robust_stress --base stress_seasonal; uv run agent/summarize.py candidate_events --base candidate_v1_full; cat agent/BUDGET.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
