{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_173","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration25 — causal historical calendar validation\n\nHypothesis: calendar gains, including the preference for stronger multipliers, should survive releases outside the repeatedly examined September/October period. The supplied calendar shows FOMC onJul29 and CPI onAug12, within the already scored historical windows. Recompute event diagnostics using only January–June prices and the May–June seasonal profile, then fit a separate July1 event artifact. The existing June–August-normalized diagnostics cannot simply be filtered by date: their seasonal normalizer was fitted later. This refit avoids that hidden lookahead.\n\nCompare original-strength and power1.5 historical event models against historical_seasonal on the two existing three-day windows endingAug01/Aug15, all assets/configurations,1000 paths, cached official scoring. Keep the original overlap convention in both event variants to isolate strength. These are retrospective robustness checks, not untouched model-selection data. Run behind robust_stress, retaining the14-worker ceiling.\n\nCalendar audit: upcoming release types/dates were read only from SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR, which explicitly includes schedules published by cutoff; no future prices or API queries were used. This audit does not license changing parameters specifically for an unseen release outcome.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/analyze_events.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"args=ap.parse_args()\\\", \\\"ap.add_argument('--end',default='2026-09-01');ap.add_argument('--table',default='seasonality.json');ap.add_argument('--suffix',default=None);args=ap.parse_args()\\\").replace(\\\"suffix='_fine' if args.fine else ''\\\", \\\"suffix=args.suffix if args.suffix is not None else ('_fine' if args.fine else '')\\\").replace(\\\"pd.Timestamp('2026-09-01',tz='UTC')\\\", \\\"pd.Timestamp(args.end,tz='UTC')\\\").replace(\\\"f.stem[5:]<'2026-09-01'\\\", \\\"f.stem[5:]<args.end\\\").replace('shape_at(r.index,asset,True)', 'shape_at(r.index,asset,True,args.table)');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('agent/fit_events.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"args=ap.parse_args();suffix='_fine' if args.fine else ''\\\", \\\"ap.add_argument('--end',default='2026-09-01');ap.add_argument('--suffix',default=None);args=ap.parse_args();suffix=args.suffix if args.suffix is not None else ('_fine' if args.fine else '')\\\").replace(\\\"x['group']=\\\", \\\"x=x[pd.to_datetime(x.time,utc=True)<pd.Timestamp(args.end,tz='UTC')]\\\\nx['group']=\\\").replace(\\\"'train_end_exclusive':'2026-09-01'\\\", \\\"'train_end_exclusive':args.end\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text().replace('def event_parameters(fine=False):', 'def event_parameters(fine=False,name=None):').replace(\\\"    name='event_multipliers_fine.json' if fine else 'event_multipliers.json'\\\", \\\"    name=name or ('event_multipliers_fine.json' if fine else 'event_multipliers.json')\\\").replace('fine=False,power=1.,exclude=()):','fine=False,power=1.,exclude=(),parameters=None):').replace('params=event_parameters(fine)[group]','params=event_parameters(fine,parameters)[group]').replace(\\\"c.get('event_exclude',()))\\\", \\\"c.get('event_exclude',()),c.get('event_table'))\\\");p.write_text(s)\nimport json\njobs=[{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/analyze_events.py','--end','2026-07-01','--table','seasonality_jul01.json','--suffix','_jul01'],'log':'agent/results/event_diagnostics_jul01.log'},{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/fit_events.py','--end','2026-07-01','--suffix','_jul01'],'log':'agent/results/event_fit_jul01.log'}]\nfor power in [1.,1.5]:\n tag='historical_events' if power==1 else 'historical_event_power'\n config={'seasonal':True,'table':'seasonality_jul01.json','events':True,'event_table':'event_multipliers_jul01.json','event_power':power}\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','research_model','--config',json.dumps(config),'--cached-prompts','--days','3','--ends','2026-08-01','2026-08-15','--workers','2'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_historical_events.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_historical_events.json --after-pid 20812 > agent/results/queue_historical_events.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
