{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_237","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration24 full combined result: latent-volatility reversion improves15/16 COM cells at float32 versus v5, mean per-asset gains0.0270%/0.0341%; CRPS2096.5230→2095.9403 and1803.7327→1803.1622. KEEP as a candidate, but defer serving promotion until independent-seed checks. Its effect is small enough that a shared random fan can create apparently consistent asset/window signs. Test the identical reversion on v3 COM at three seeds using the controls already generated for the Sobol audit; this isolates the stochastic-law change without paying for duplicate controls. Full v5 validation above measures interaction with robust variance.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\njobs=[]\nfor seed in [20261011,11,37]:\n tag=f'reversion_v3_seed{seed}'\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v3_research','--config',json.dumps({'mix_revert':True}),'--assets','XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500','--formats','24h','--workers','2','--seed',str(seed)],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_reversion_seeds.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_reversion_seeds.json > agent/results/queue_reversion_seeds.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
