{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_153","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration22 persistence control completed: only2/10 cells improve; mean changes+0.2380%/+0.0210%. DISCARD hourly persistence. Thus the favorable Chronos result is not reproduced by simply blending the latest complete-hour variance. This does not prove pretrained superiority to every classical model; it rules out this particular simple explanation.\n\nIteration9 next combined test registered: add Chronos quarter-blend to candidate_v3 for crypto1h on both full ten-day windows. Compare against candidate_v2_full (v3 is exactly identical for1h), holding fast15, clock, event kernels and mixture0.35 fixed. Require favorable means in both windows and predominantly favorable asset cells. Run only after the existing GPU suite exits; one GPU worker throughout.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('agent/candidate_v3.py');s=p.read_text();needle=\\\"'_seed':seed}\\\";assert s.count(needle)==1;s=s.replace(needle,\\\"'_seed':seed,**__import__('json').loads(os.environ.get('MODEL_CONFIG','{}'))}\\\")\nPath('agent/candidate_v3_research.py').write_text(s.replace('Candidate v2 plus validated group-specific shrinkage and profile refresh.','Research-only configurable ablation of candidate v3.'))\njobs=[{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','chronos_v3_full','--model','candidate_v3_research','--research','--config',json.dumps({'chronos':True}),'--days','10','--ends','2026-09-19','2026-10-11','--formats','1h','--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--workers','1'],'log':'agent/results/chronos_v3_full_suite.log'}]\nPath('agent/queue_chronos_full.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_chronos_full.json --after-pid 13859 > agent/results/queue_chronos_full.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_219","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/chronos_vol.py');s=p.read_text().replace('def pipeline():', \\\"def pipeline(model_name='chronos-t5-tiny'):\\\").replace(\\\"str(Path(__file__).parent/'models/chronos-t5-tiny')\\\", \\\"str(Path(__file__).parent/'models'/model_name)\\\").replace('def predict_hourly(asset,origin,seed,values):', \\\"def predict_hourly(asset,origin,seed,values,model_name='chronos-t5-tiny'):\\\").replace('    model=pipeline()', '    model=pipeline(model_name)').replace('def forecast_variance(frame,asset,future,seed,persistence=False):', \\\"def forecast_variance(frame,asset,future,seed,persistence=False,model_name='chronos-t5-tiny'):\\\").replace('forecast=predict_hourly(asset,str(origin),seed,values)', 'forecast=predict_hourly(asset,str(origin),seed,values,model_name)');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"c.get('hourly_persistence',False))\\\", \\\"c.get('hourly_persistence',False),c.get('chronos_model','chronos-t5-tiny'))\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > agent/benchmark_chronos_small.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Single-GPU capacity probe; queued behind the existing model job.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport time,json,os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np\nfrom chronos_vol import pipeline,predict_hourly\nimport torch\nseed=int(os.environ.get('SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED','20261011'));torch.manual_seed(seed)\nvalues=tuple(np.exp(np.sin(np.arange(144)/12))*1e-6)\nt=time.perf_counter();pipeline('chronos-t5-small');load=time.perf_counter()-t\nlatencies=[];forecasts=[]\nfor i in range(3):\n predict_hourly.cache_clear();t=time.perf_counter()\n forecasts.append(predict_hourly('TEST','origin',seed,values,'chronos-t5-small'))\n torch.cuda.synchronize();latencies.append(time.perf_counter()-t)\nassert all(np.array_equal(forecasts[0],f) for f in forecasts[1:])\nresult={'load_seconds':load,'predict_seconds':latencies,'first_response_seconds':load+latencies[0],'max_allocated_gib':torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated()/2**30,'repeatable':True}\nPath('agent/results/chronos_small_latency.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2));print(result)\nif load+latencies[0]>5 or max(latencies)>5:raise SystemExit('Preregistered practical latency gate failed')\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\njobs=[{'cmd':['uv','run','--group','research','agent/benchmark_chronos_small.py'],'log':'agent/results/chronos_small_latency.log'},{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','chronos_small_fast15','--model','research_model','--research','--config',json.dumps({'seasonal':True,'fast_half':15,'chronos':True,'chronos_model':'chronos-t5-small'}),'--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','1h','--workers','1'],'log':'agent/results/chronos_small_fast15_suite.log'}]\nPath('agent/queue_chronos_small.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_chronos_small.json --after-pid 20277 > agent/results/queue_chronos_small.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_255","type":"agent_message","text":"The finer profiles and extra refreshes each passed their full-window checks, and I’m testing their combination. Sobol also retained a small gain across all three seeds for commodities/equities. I’ll add a conventional GARCH comparison alongside the pretrained models to test whether a learned volatility update rule offers a cheaper improvement.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_256","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration35 — a classical learned volatility recursion\n\nHypothesis: a variance-targeted GARCH(1,1) update may improve one-hour volatility forecasts beyond fixed EWMA weights, providing a useful classical comparison for Chronos. Normalize minute squared returns by the known seasonal profile and a strictly lagged finite-seven-day EWMA level. Fit only the GARCH response and persistence coefficients by Gaussian quasi-likelihood, with persistence constrained to0.90–0.999 and positive weights. Missing returns receive only the model's mean-reversion update; no prices are filled.\n\nFirst fit June–July using the pre-July seasonal artifact and assess August quasi-likelihood as a causal diagnostic. Then refit June–August using the pre-September seasonal artifact before official September/October scoring. Neither likelihood result is CRPS. Compare1000-path one-hour forecasts against fast15 on all five crypto assets and both initial windows. Reject if either official mean regresses or most assets fail to improve; no24h GARCH inference is selected from this experiment. Check finite-context sensitivity and serving latency before any combined promotion.\nEOF\ncat > agent/garch_vol.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Variance-targeted GARCH experiment; no prices are imputed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.signal import lfilter\nfrom numba import njit\n\ndef finite_ewma(values,half=4320,window=10080):\n    values=np.asarray(values,dtype=float);ok=np.isfinite(values);rate=2**(-1/half)\n    num=lfilter([1.],[1.,-rate],np.where(ok,values,0.));den=lfilter([1.],[1.,-rate],ok.astype(float))\n    if len(values)>window:\n        num[window:]-=rate**window*num[:-window].copy()\n        den[window:]-=rate**window*den[:-window].copy()\n    return np.divide(num,den,out=np.full(len(values),1e-8),where=den>1e-12)\n\n@njit(cache=True)\ndef filter_state(normalized,alpha,persistence,loss_mask):\n    state=1.;loss=0.;n=0\n    for i in range(len(normalized)):\n        value=normalized[i]\n        state=max(state,1e-10)\n        if np.isfinite(value):\n            if loss_mask[i]:loss+=np.log(state)+value/state;n+=1\n            state=(1-persistence)+alpha*value+(persistence-alpha)*state\n        else:\n            state=(1-persistence)+persistence*state\n    return state,loss/max(n,1)\n\ndef prepare(frame,asset,shape_name='seasonality.json',clock=False):\n    from research_model import shape_at,clock_at\n    close=frame.close.astype(float)\n    close=close.reindex(pd.date_range(close.index[0],close.index[-1],freq='min'))\n    shape=shape_at(close.index,asset,True,shape_name)\n    if clock:shape*=clock_at(close.index,asset,1)\n    values=np.log(close).diff().to_numpy()**2/shape\n    level=finite_ewma(values)\n    previous=np.concatenate([np.array([1e-8]),level[:-1]])\n    return close.index,values,level,values/np.maximum(previous,1e-14)\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\ndef parameters():\n    return json.loads((Path(__file__).parent/'garch.json').read_text())['assets']\n\ndef forecast(frame,asset,future,shape_name='seasonality.json',clock=False):\n    index,values,level,z=prepare(frame,asset,shape_name,clock)\n    fitted=parameters()[asset];state,_=filter_state(z,fitted['alpha'],fitted['persistence'],np.zeros(len(z),dtype=np.bool_))\n    elapsed=np.asarray((future-index[-1]).total_seconds())/60\n    return level[-1]*(1+(state-1)*fitted['persistence']**np.maximum(elapsed-1,0))\nPY\ncat > agent/fit_garch.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Fit two stationary GARCH coefficients; all CRPS tests remain official.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import default_store_root\nfrom garch_vol import prepare,filter_state,finite_ewma\nassets=['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE'];out={'train_end_exclusive':'2026-09-01','assets':{},'diagnostics':{}}\nfor asset in assets:\n files=[p for p in sorted(default_store_root(asset).glob('date=*.parquet')) if '2026-05-25'<=p.stem[5:]<'2026-09-01']\n frame=pd.concat([pd.read_parquet(p,columns=['timestamp','close']) for p in files]).set_index('timestamp').sort_index()\n for phase,table,end in [('diagnostic','seasonality_jul01.json','2026-08-01'),('final','seasonality.json','2026-09-01')]:\n  index,y,level,z=prepare(frame,asset,table)\n  mask=np.asarray((index>=pd.Timestamp('2026-06-01',tz='UTC'))&(index<pd.Timestamp(end,tz='UTC')))\n  def objective(theta):\n   persistence,fraction=theta\n   return filter_state(z,persistence*fraction,persistence,mask)[1]\n  fits=[minimize(objective,start,method='L-BFGS-B',bounds=[(.90,.999),(.001,.30)],options={'maxiter':80,'ftol':1e-10}) for start in [[.99,.05],[.997,.02]]]\n  fit=min(fits,key=lambda f:f.fun);p,f=fit.x;values={'alpha':float(p*f),'persistence':float(p),'beta':float(p-p*f),'fit_nll':float(fit.fun),'converged':bool(fit.success)}\n  if phase=='diagnostic':\n   validation=np.asarray(index>=pd.Timestamp('2026-08-01',tz='UTC'))\n   values['august_nll']=float(filter_state(z,p*f,p,validation)[1])\n   fast=.6*finite_ewma(y,15)+.25*finite_ewma(y,360)+.15*finite_ewma(y,4320)\n   ratio=np.concatenate([[1.],fast[:-1]/np.maximum(level[:-1],1e-14)])\n   valid=validation&np.isfinite(z)\n   values['august_fast15_nll']=float(np.mean(np.log(ratio[valid])+z[valid]/ratio[valid]))\n   out['diagnostics'][asset]=values\n  else:out['assets'][asset]=values\n  print(asset,phase,values,flush=True)\nPath('agent/garch.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/fit_garch.py > agent/results/garch_fit.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
