{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_280","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration39 — robust hourly-level control and forecast diagnostics\n\nHypothesis: the similar tiny/small forecasts may derive much of their benefit from moving toward a robust recent hourly variance level. The earlier persistence and EWMA controls do not test that explanation. Add a last144-complete-hours median variance control with the same25% blend and clipping, on all five crypto assets and both initial windows at1000 paths. Require favorable means and most cells, and compare directly with Chronos before attributing gains to pretrained dynamics.\n\nSeparately measure learned/base ratios, clipping rates and learned/median ratios on representative actual prompt contexts for both public checkpoints. These are forecast diagnostics, not CRPS evaluations; no future outcomes are needed. Queue this one GPU job behind the current small-model scoring job. The CPU median-control suite waits for the GARCH-blend workers, preserving the shared hardware ceiling.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/chronos_vol.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"        estimate=hourly.ewm(halflife=6).mean().iloc[-1] if persistence=='ewma' else hourly.dropna().iloc[-1]\\\", \\\"        if persistence=='median':estimate=hourly.median()\\\\n        elif persistence=='ewma':estimate=hourly.ewm(halflife=6).mean().iloc[-1]\\\\n        else:estimate=hourly.dropna().iloc[-1]\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text();needle=\\\"        blend=c.get('chronos_blend',.25)\\\";assert s.count(needle)==1;s=s.replace(needle,\\\"        if c.get('_forecast_diagnostics') is not None:\\\\n            c['_forecast_diagnostics'].update(base=base.copy(),learned=learned.copy())\\\\n\\\"+needle);p.write_text(s)\nimport json\njobs=[{'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','hourly_median','--model','research_model','--config',json.dumps({'seasonal':True,'fast_half':15,'hourly_persistence':'median'}),'--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','1h','--workers','2'],'log':'agent/results/hourly_median_suite.log'}]\nPath('agent/queue_hourly_median.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\ncat > agent/diagnose_chronos_forecasts.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Forecast-level diagnostics only; no scores or future outcomes are used.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom predict import load_minute_prices,WORKSPACE,context_end\nfrom research_model import simulate_config\nfrom chronos_vol import forecast_variance\nseed=int(os.environ.get('SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED','20261011'));rows=[]\nfor model in ['chronos-t5-tiny','chronos-t5-small']:\n for asset in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE']:\n  for end in ['2026-09-16','2026-10-10']:\n   scores=pd.read_parquet(f'agent/results/fast15/{asset}_1h_{end}.parquet',columns=['start_time'])\n   times=pd.to_datetime(scores.start_time,utc=True).sort_values().drop_duplicates()\n   times=times.groupby(times.dt.floor('6h')).first()\n   frame=load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE/'market_data',asset,times.min()-pd.Timedelta(days=7),times.max())\n   for t in times:\n    context=frame.loc[t-pd.Timedelta(days=7):context_end(t,3600)];sink={}\n    c={'seasonal':True,'fast_half':15,'chronos':True,'chronos_model':model,'_seed':seed,'_forecast_diagnostics':sink}\n    simulate_config(asset,t.isoformat(),60,3600,17,context,np.random.default_rng(seed),c)\n    future=pd.date_range(t+pd.Timedelta(minutes=1),periods=60,freq='min')\n    median=forecast_variance(context,asset,future,seed,'median')\n    ratio=sink['learned']/sink['base']\n    rows.append({'model':model,'asset':asset,'end':end,'start_time':str(t),'ratio_mean':float(ratio.mean()),'lower_clip_share':float(np.mean(ratio<.25)),'upper_clip_share':float(np.mean(ratio>4)),'learned_over_median':float(np.mean(sink['learned']/median))})\n  print(model,asset,'complete',flush=True)\nx=pd.DataFrame(rows);x.to_csv('agent/results/chronos_forecast_diagnostics.csv',index=False)\nprint(x.groupby(['model','asset'])[['ratio_mean','lower_clip_share','upper_clip_share','learned_over_median']].mean().round(5).to_string())\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_hourly_median.json --after-pid 39278 > agent/results/queue_hourly_median.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
