{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_263","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > agent/benchmark_chronos_serving.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Identical fresh-process serving benchmarks for public Chronos checkpoints.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport argparse,time,os,json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--model',choices=['chronos-t5-tiny','chronos-t5-small'],required=True);a=p.parse_args()\nbegin=time.perf_counter()\nfrom chronos_vol import pipeline,predict_hourly\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd,torch\nfrom chronos import ChronosPipeline\nimport research_model\nseed=int(os.environ.get('SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED','20261011'));torch.manual_seed(seed);torch.cuda.init();torch.cuda.reset_peak_memory_stats()\nframework=time.perf_counter()-begin\nbefore=time.perf_counter();pipeline(a.model);load=time.perf_counter()-before\n# Serving receives context from its caller; snapshot I/O is excluded from model latency.\nfrom predict import load_minute_prices,WORKSPACE,context_end\nt=pd.Timestamp('2026-09-15T12:00:00Z')\nframe=load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE/'market_data','BTC',t-pd.Timedelta(days=7),t).loc[:context_end(t,3600)]\nos.environ['MODEL_CONFIG']=json.dumps({'seasonal':True,'fast_half':15,'chronos':True,'chronos_model':a.model})\nlatencies=[];first=None\nfor _ in range(3):\n predict_hourly.cache_clear();before=time.perf_counter()\n out=research_model.simulate('BTC',t.isoformat(),60,3600,1000,frame)\n torch.cuda.synchronize();latencies.append(time.perf_counter()-before)\n paths=np.asarray(out[2:]);assert paths.shape==(1000,61) and np.isfinite(paths).all()\n if first is None:first=paths\n else:assert np.array_equal(first,paths)\nresult={'model':a.model,'framework_startup_seconds':framework,'model_load_seconds':load,'simulate_seconds':latencies,'cold_response_seconds':framework+load+latencies[0],'max_allocated_gib':torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated()/2**30,'paths':1000,'repeatable':True}\nPath(f'agent/results/{a.model}_serving_latency.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2));print(result)\nif result['cold_response_seconds']>=60 or max(latencies[1:])>=5:raise SystemExit('Revised latency gate failed')\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\njobs=[]\nfor model in ['chronos-t5-tiny','chronos-t5-small']:\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','--group','research','agent/benchmark_chronos_serving.py','--model',model],'log':f'agent/results/{model}_serving_latency.log'})\nold=json.loads(Path('agent/queue_chronos_small.json').read_text());jobs.append(old[1])\nPath('agent/queue_chronos_capacity.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_chronos_capacity.json > agent/results/queue_chronos_capacity.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_244","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration32 — local width calibration\n\nHypothesis: rejecting the earlier15% narrowing does not establish that the current combined model is locally calibrated. Test only0.95 and1.05 global volatility multipliers around v5, one at a time, on the two full ten-day windows at1000 paths and float32. The Gaussian local-curvature heuristic predicts only about0.06% loss for a5% width error near optimum, so this is a modest refinement rather than a claim of large upside. Compare crypto with identical v4 controls and COM with v5 controls. Require both window means and most favorable cells within a configuration before selecting a group-specific scale; do not choose per asset or extend a grid merely to find a favorable result.\n\nComparator safeguard: add an explicit COM control override and reject differing prompt counts, so composed v5 controls remain transparent and windows of unequal length cannot be silently compared just because their end date matches. Allocate the three CPU workers released by the completed v4 suite.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/summarize.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"p.add_argument('--base',default='baseline');\\\", \\\"p.add_argument('--base',default='baseline');p.add_argument('--base-com');\\\").replace(\\\"[a.base]+a.tags\\\", \\\"[a.base]+([a.base_com] if a.base_com else [])+a.tags\\\").replace(\\\"base=df[df.tag==a.base].set_index(['asset','fmt','end']).crps\\\", \\\"controls=df[df.tag==a.base]\\\\nif a.base_com:controls=pd.concat([controls[controls.config\"'!='\"'COM_EQU_24H'],df[(df.tag==a.base_com)&(df.config=='COM_EQU_24H')]])\\\\ncontrols=controls.set_index(['asset','fmt','end']);base=controls.crps\\\\nif a.base_com:print('Controls:',a.base,'for crypto;',a.base_com,'for COM')\\\").replace(\\\"d=d[d.base.notna()]\\\", \\\"d=d[d.base.notna()]\\\\n for r in d.it