{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_287","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; sed -n '270,390p' agent/CAMPAIGN.md; git status --short; ps -eo pid,ppid,etime,args | rg 'run_suite|queue_|diagnose_chronos|predict.py'\"","aggregated_output":"# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 40.44 / 100.00 USD (40%)\n- Time   : 2.1 h elapsed, 15.9 h remaining (12%)\n- Phase  : normal\n\n## Harness notes\n\n- GPU: 28 min busy so far, peak memory 0.5 GiB\n  this file appears (result in BUDGET.md) — fix it if the check fails.\n- `suggestions.md`: anything that falls outside your scope.\n- you must commit all deliverables to your workspace git repo before the deadline.\n\n## Method (your choice, but recommended)\n\nYou choose your own research questions, hypotheses, splits, and criteria. What works here:\nwrite the hypothesis BEFORE the experiment, pre-registered kill thresholds, validation on 2\nwindows of opposite regimes (within the limits of the snapshot), one variable at a time,\nfrequent commits. Watch out for the edges of eval windows: only backtest windows fully covered\nby the snapshot. Lessons earlier agents paid for:\n\n- **Price a residual before fitting it.** For a Gaussian fan, expected CRPS at scale σ against\n  the right σ* is about 1 + ¼·(ln σ/σ*)² times the optimum: a ±20 % global scale error costs about\n  1 %, and a width correction across buckets can gain at most about ¼ of the variance of the\n  log width ratios. A minute of arithmetic tells you whether a day of sweeping can pay.\n- **Test a feature by what it adds to a fast EWMA of realized volatility**, not by its own\n  predictive power. Range estimators, volume, trade counts and the leverage effect act on future\n  volatility through realized volatility, which the EWMA has already priced. What it cannot hold\n  is information outside the context: the calendar, and anything older than the 7 days\n  `simulate()` receives.\n- **Validate an event effect leave-one-event-out.** A type occurs 8 to 12 times a year, so a\n  multiplier fitted and tested on the same releases is in-sample.\n- **Check what `simulate()` can see before building on it**: one asset's 7-day context per\n  call, nothing else. A feature that needs another asset's current prices cannot be served.\n- **Count the asset-window cells where a change helps**, across disjoint windows, not only its\n  average: a small gain signed the same way in most cells survives; a larger one that flips sign\n  between windows is noise.\n\n## Resuming after a crash\n\nIf you restart with no context: reread this file, then `BUDGET.md`, then your `journal.md`,\nand continue where you left off.\nM  .gitignore\nA  agent/benchmark_chronos_serving.py\nA  agent/benchmark_chronos_small.py\nA  agent/candidate_v5.py\nA  agent/candidate_v5_research.py\nA  agent/candidate_v6.py\nA  agent/candidate_v7.py\nA  agent/candidate_v7_research.py\nA  agent/check_precision.py\nMM agent/chronos_vol.py\nA  agent/fit_garch.py\nM  agent/fit_seasonality.py\nA  agent/garch.json\nA  agent/garch_vol.py\nMM agent/journal.md\nM  agent/modeling.py\nA  agent/models/chronos-t5-small/README.md\nA  agent/models/chronos-t5-small/config.json\nA  agent/models/chronos-t5-small/generation_config.json\nA  agent/models/chronos-t5-small/model.safetensors\nA  agent/models/chronos-t5-small/provenance.json\nA  agent/queue_chronos_capacity.json\nA  agent/queue_chronos_small.json\nA  agent/queue_fine_com.json\nA  agent/queue_fine_seasonal.json\nA  agent/queue_local_scale.json\nA  agent/queue_reversion_seeds.json\nA  agent/queue_rolling.json\nA  agent/queue_sep_late.json\nA  agent/queue_sobol_com.json\nA  agent/queue_v6.json\nM  agent/report.md\nMM agent/research_model.py\nA  agent/results/baseline_float32/SP500_24h_2026-10-11.json\nM  agent/results/baseline_float32/SP500_24h_2026-10-11.log\nA  agent/results/baseline_float32/SP500_24h_2026-10-11.parquet\nA  agent/results/baseline_float32/SPCX_24h_2026-1