{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_282","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration40 — quiet-session floor in the refined COM model\n\nHypothesis: the earlier low-shrinkage COM experiment mixed large weekend gains with weekday losses. The now-validated fine profiles, robust level estimator and Sobol sampler may change that tradeoff, and a weekend-only floor adjustment may isolate it. On v7, test two predeclared settings: global2% shrinkage, and10% weekday/2% weekend shrinkage. Compare both against the existing10%/10% control on the full September/October windows at1000 paths,float32. Do not change scale or any other parameter.\n\nRequire gains in both configuration means and mostly favorable asset cells before considering either; report weekday/weekend daily effects, and validate any retained setting on the added late-September period before final use. No additional shrinkage grid will be inferred from the favorable stress result. Table lookup accepts a two-row shrinkage vector for this experiment, with exact old-scalar parity checked first. Queue behind the existing v7 COM workers.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text();old='''    if shrink\"'!=.1 and arr.shape[0]==2:\n        raw=np.maximum((arr-.1)/.9,1e-5)\n        arr=(1-shrink)*raw+shrink'\"''';new='''    strength=np.asarray(shrink,dtype=float)\n    if strength.ndim:strength=strength.reshape(2,1)\n    if arr.shape[0]==2 and np.any(strength\"'!=.1):\n        raw=np.maximum((arr-.1)/.9,1e-5)\n        arr=(1-strength)*raw+strength'\"''';assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new);p.write_text(s)\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys,numpy as np,pandas as pd,json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nimport modeling,research_model\nidx=pd.date_range('2026-09-01',periods=10080,freq='min',tz='UTC')\nfor asset in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500']:\n for name in ['seasonality.json','seasonality_fine.json']:\n  for shrink in [.1,.02]:assert np.array_equal(modeling.shape_at(idx,asset,True,name,shrink),research_model.shape_at(idx,asset,True,name,shrink))\nprint('Scalar shrinkage unchanged exactly on52 asset/table/strength combinations')\njobs=[]\nfor tag,strength in [('floor02_v7_float32',.02),('weekend_floor_v7_float32',[.1,.02])]:\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v7_research','--config',json.dumps({'seasonal_shrink':strength}),'--prediction-dtype','float32','--days','10','--ends','2026-09-19','2026-10-11','--assets','XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500','--formats','24h','--workers','2'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_quiet_floor.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_quiet_floor.json --after-pid 38894 > agent/results/queue_quiet_floor.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"Scalar shrinkage unchanged exactly on52 asset/table/strength combinations\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_334","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration46 — forecast decay versus estimation memory\n\nHypothesis: the selected15-minute estimation half-life need not imply the correct four-hour forward variance-reversion half-life. The latter has remained fixed while estimation memory changed. For crypto1h only, test a60-minute forward half-life and an effectively constant forecast (half-life1e12 minutes), each against v7's240-minute control. All estimates, distributions, event layers and random paths stay identical. This brackets stronger versus negligible forward reversion without changing the history estimator.\n\nScore both full windows,1000 paths,float32,official cached scorer. Require both means and most asset cells; reject an option on either mean regression. No finer sweep follows. Any retained decay must be measured with the selected hourly predictor and on added dates. Reserve the two CPU workers of the quiet-floor queue after its completion; total maximum14CPU/oneGPU unchanged.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\njobs=[]\nfor tag,half in [('forecast_decay60_v7_full',60),('forecast_constant_v7_full',1e12)]:\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v7_research','--config',json.dumps({'revert_half':half}),'--cached-prompts','--prediction-dtype','float32','--days','10','--ends','2026-09-19','2026-10-11','--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','1h','--workers','2'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_forecast_decay.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_forecast_decay.json --after-pid 44331 > agent/results/queue_forecast_decay.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
