{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_352","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration49 — state-dependent mixture confirmation and width interaction\n\nThe adaptive-mixture full-window test has nine favorable completed cells, with all five September assets improving (mean0.1641%); no promotion before the tenth cell. Prepare two independent follow-ups: adaptive mixture on the added Sep23–30 period against the unchanged v5/v7 one-hour control, then adaptive mixture plus0.95 scale on both full windows against adaptive alone. Require both full-window means and most cells for the interaction, and favorable added-period mean/majority for the shape change. Keep the formula fixed; no coefficient fitting to the scored dates. Three workers wait for the registered adaptive suite, preserving the14-worker ceiling.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\njobs=[]\nfor tag,cfg,days,ends in [('sep_late_adaptive_mix',{'adaptive_mix':True},8,['2026-10-01']),('adaptive_mix_scale95_v7_full',{'adaptive_mix':True,'scale':.95},10,['2026-09-19','2026-10-11'])]:\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v8_research','--config',json.dumps(cfg),'--cached-prompts','--prediction-dtype','float32','--days',str(days),'--ends',*ends,'--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','1h','--workers','3'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_adaptive_followup.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_adaptive_followup.json --after-pid 55426 > agent/results/queue_adaptive_followup.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_327","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration42 low-floor confirmation: all8 added-period COM cells improve, mean0.6644%, CRPS1869.7969→1857.8117. Combined with16/16 full-window cells and19/20 daily means, KEEP global0.02 floor. Descriptive two-day block intervals for daily percentage changes are[-1.145,-0.141]% and[-2.587,-0.274]%; these do not correct repeated selection. Weekend-only and uniform-width interaction comparisons still determine the final combination.\n\n## Iteration45 — state-dependent volatility uncertainty\n\nHypothesis: disagreement between recent and long-memory variance forecasts should widen uncertainty about volatility itself, rather than simply shift the central variance. On v7 crypto1h only, replace fixed log-volatility std0.35 with sqrt(0.35\"'^2 +0.10*log(initial/long)''^2), capped0.55. Preserve the mixture'\"'s unit second moment, all variance forecasts and random draws. This changes tail/central-mass shape when recent and long variance disagree; it does not use future observations or train a residual target.\n\nTest exactly this one functional form,1000 paths,float32,both full windows against unchanged v7(=v4 for1h). Require both configuration means and most asset cells to improve; otherwise discard without tuning the coefficient/cap. A favorable result would still need combination with the selected hourly predictor and additional-period validation. Queue three CPU workers after the floor-interaction queue, preserving maximum14 and oneGPU.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text();old=\\\"    mix=c.get('mix',0)\\\\n\\\";new=\\\"    mix=c.get('mix',0)\\\\n    if mix and c.get('adaptive_mix',False):\\\\n        disagreement=np.log(max(initial,1e-14)/max(long,1e-14))\\\\n        mix=min(.55,float(np.sqrt(mix*mix+.10*disagreement*disagreement)))\\\\n\\\";assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new);p.write_text(s)\njob={'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag','adaptive_mix_v7_full','--model','candidate_v7_research','--config',json.dumps({'adaptive_mix':True}),'--cached-prompts','--prediction-dtype','float32','--days','10','--ends','2026-09-19','2026-10-11','--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','1h','--workers','3'],'log':'agent/results/adaptive_mix_v7_full_suite.log'}\nPath('agent/queue_adaptive_mix.json').write_text(json.dumps([job],indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_adaptive_mix.json --after-pid 54714 > agent/results/queue_adaptive_mix.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_344","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration48 — variance-clock Brownian bridge sampling\n\nHypothesis: Sobol's limited low-dimensional accuracy should prioritize cumulative path returns, not successive minute shocks. Generate Gaussian paths using a Brownian bridge on the model's deterministic cumulative-variance clock, assigning the first Sobol coordinate to path-level volatility and the remaining early coordinates to terminal/coarse path structure. This preserves the independent-normal increment law analytically while changing finite-ensemble integration error. Existing direct Sobol crypto failures do not test this coordinate construction.\n\nBefore CRPS, verify the bridge's exact linear covariance identity at1,7,60,288 steps with strongly heterogeneous variances; this checks distribution preservation without a sampling-based tolerance. Then compare v3+bridge against existing v3 controls on both initial windows and seeds11/37, all three configurations,1000 paths,float32. Require all four seed/window means and most cells within a configuration. No claim from a single lucky fan. Retained groups need default-seed full-window tests against the selected generator, giving a third independent seed and current-model interaction check. Allocate the four CPU workers released by the completed added-period scale test. OneGPU job continues independently; maximum14CPU.\nEOF\ncat > agent/qmc_bridge.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Linear Brownian bridge on an arbitrary deterministic variance clock.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom collections import deque\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef bridge_normals(normal, sig):\n    normal=np.asarray(normal,dtype=float)\n    sig=np.asarray(sig,dtype=float)\n    steps=len(sig)\n    if normal.shape[1]\"'!=steps or np.any(sig<=0):raise ValueError('\"'Bridge requires positive per-step scales and matching normals')\n    clock=np.r_[0.,np.cumsum(sig*sig)]\n    path=np.zeros((normal.shape[0],steps+1))\n    path[:,-1]=np.sqrt(clock[-1])*normal[:,0]\n    pending=deque([(0,steps)]);coordinate=1\n    while pending:\n        left,right=pending.popleft()\n        if right-left<=1:continue\n        middle=(left+right)//2\n        before=clock[middle]-clock[left];after=clock[right]-clock[middle];total=before+after\n        path[:,middle]=(after*path[:,left]+before*path[:,right])/total+np.sqrt(before*after/total)*normal[:,coordinate]\n        coordinate+=1\n        pending.extend([(left,middle),(middle,right)])\n    assert coordinate==steps\n    return np.diff(path,axis=1)/sig\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"if c.get('sampler')=='sobol':\\\",\\\"if c.get('sampler') in ['sobol','sobol_bridge']:\\\")\nold=\\\"        z=normal[:,:steps];mixture_normal=normal[:,-1:]\\\"\nnew=\\\"\\\"\\\"        if c.get('sampler')=='sobol_bridge':\n            from qmc_bridge import bridge_normals\n            mixture_normal=normal[:,:1]\n            z=bridge_normals(normal[:,1:],sig)\n        else:z=normal[:,:steps];mixture_normal=normal[:,-1:]\\\"\\\"\\\"\nassert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new);p.write_text(s)\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys,numpy as np\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nfrom qmc_bridge import bridge_normals\nfor steps in [1,7,60,288]:\n sig=np.exp(np.linspace(-3,3,steps));z=bridge_normals(np.eye(steps),sig)\n error=np.max(np.abs(z.T@z-np.eye(steps)))\n assert error<1e-9\n print(steps,'covariance identity max error',error)\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\njobs=[]\nfor seed in [11,37]:\n tag=f'bridge_v3_seed{seed}'\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v3_research','--config',json.dumps({'sampler':'sobol_bridge'}),'--seed',str(seed),'--cached-prompts','--prediction-dtype','float32','--workers','4'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_bridge.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_bridge.json > agent/results/queue_bridge.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"1 covariance identity max error 0.0\n7 covariance identity max error 4.440892098500626e-16\n60 covariance identity max error 8.881784197001252e-16\n288 covariance identity max error 2.7755575615628914e-15\n","exit_code":143,"status":"failed"}}
