{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_391","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration58 confirms the counterexample under bridge sampling: July improves0.0723%, August regresses0.0871%, with XRP+0.73% and only3/5 August cells improved. DISCARD symmetric adaptive mixture from serving. Preserve it as a research candidate and keep its completed favorable and unfavorable results. V9 is revised to v8+one-hour bridge ONLY before nomination; the earlier adaptive freezing step is explicitly withdrawn. The asymmetric calm-state hypothesis is a separate registered experiment and earns no promotion from this failure.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/candidate_v9.py');s=p.read_text();Path('agent/candidate_withdrawn_symmetric.py').write_text(s.replace('Candidate v9:','Withdrawn candidate:'))\ns=s.replace('Candidate v9: v8 plus adaptive one-hour volatility mixtures and Brownian bridge sampling.','Candidate v9: v8 plus validated one-hour Brownian bridge sampling.').replace(\\\"            'adaptive_mix':short,\\\\n\\\",'');p.write_text(s)\nPath('agent/candidate_v9_research.py').write_text(s.replace('Candidate v9: v8 plus validated one-hour Brownian bridge sampling.','Research-only configurable ablation of candidate v9.').replace(\\\"'_seed':seed}\\\",\\\"'_seed':seed,**__import__('json').loads(os.environ.get('MODEL_CONFIG','{}'))}\\\"))\np=Path('agent/modeling.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"            'adaptive_mix':short,\\\\n\\\",'');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
