{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_396","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration60 diagnostics: most adjacent standardized returns have small negative correlations. After fixed50% shrinkage, implied long-horizon standard-deviation factors are0.9856–1.0008 for crypto24h,0.9850–1.0091 for COM, and0.9895–0.9961 for crypto1h. XAU is consistently positive; BTC/XRP minute correlations and HYPE five-minute correlation change sign across the two training subperiods. This is a modest horizon-shape hypothesis, not evidence for a large forecast gain.\n\n## Iteration61 — covariance law at fixed base-step variance\n\nUse the prevalidation shrunken correlations in a stationary Gaussian AR(1) innovation law, preserving unit variance at every individual step and zero forecast mean. Keep the observed-price start, volatility forecasts, mixtures and sampling unchanged. No conditional-return drift is added. Apply only when the requested step matches the fitted1-/5-minute lag; other step sizes retain independent innovations.\n\nValidate exact covariance algebra before official scoring, then compare against v9 on all three configurations across both full windows,1000 paths,float32. Require both means and most asset cells within a configuration; no per-asset score-based selection. A retained group needs added-period confirmation. Four CPU workers fit within the current10-worker maximum including the reserved cached-interaction workers.\nEOF\ncat > agent/path_dependence.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Stationary Gaussian return dependence with unchanged per-step variance.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.signal import lfilter\n\ndef correlated_normals(normal,rho):\n    if not -1<rho<1:raise ValueError('Stationary correlation must be between -1 and1')\n    if rho==0:return normal\n    innovations=np.asarray(normal)*np.sqrt(1-rho*rho)\n    innovations[:,0]=normal[:,0]\n    return lfilter([1.],[1.,-rho],innovations,axis=1)\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text();needle=\\\"    if c.get('empirical',False):\\\";assert needle in s;s=s.replace(needle,\\\"    if c.get('return_ar1',False) and time_increment==lag*60:\\\\n        from path_dependence import correlated_normals\\\\n        z=correlated_normals(z,float(table('autocorrelation.json')[asset][str(lag)]))\\\\n\\\"+needle);p.write_text(s)\np=Path('agent/summarize.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"p.add_argument('--base-com');\\\",\\\"p.add_argument('--base-com');p.add_argument('--base-short');\\\").replace(\\\"([a.base_com] if a.base_com else [])+a.tags\\\",\\\"([a.base_com] if a.base_com else [])+([a.base_short] if a.base_short else [])+a.tags\\\")\nneedle=\\\"controls=controls.set_index(['asset','fmt','end']);base=controls.crps\\\";s=s.replace(needle,\\\"if a.base_short:controls=pd.concat([controls[controls.config\"'!='\"'CRYPTO_1H'],df[(df.tag==a.base_short)&(df.config=='CRYPTO_1H')]])\\\\n\\\"+needle)\ns=s.replace(\\\"if a.base_com:print('Controls:',a.base,'for crypto;',a.base_com,'for COM')\\\",\\\"if a.base_com or a.base_short:print('Controls:',a.base,'default;',a.base_com,'COM override;',a.base_short,'1h override')\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys,numpy as np\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nfrom path_dependence import correlated_normals\nfor steps in [7,60]:\n for rho in [-.1,-.015,.009,0.]:\n  z=correlated_normals(np.eye(steps),rho);expected=rho**np.abs(np.arange(steps)[:,None]-np.arange(steps)[None,:])\n  assert np.max(np.abs(z.T@z-expected))<1e-12\nprint('Exact stationary covariance and unit step variance:8 cases passed')\nPY\nuv run agent/run_suite.py --tag return_ar1_v9_full --model candidate_v9_research --config '{\\\"return_ar1\\\":true}' --cached-prompts --prediction-dtype float32 --days 10 --ends 2026-09-19 2026-10-11 --workers 4 > agent/results/return_ar1_v9_full_suite.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_