{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_413","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -e\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,pandas as pd\nrows=[]\nfor new,base in [('scale95_v5_float32','candidate_v4_float32'),('sep_late_scale95','sep_late_v5'),('historical_v9_crypto24h','historical_crypto24_scale1')]:\n for f in (Path('agent/results')/new).glob('*_24h_*.json'):\n  asset,fmt,end=f.stem.split('_')\n  if asset not in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE']:continue\n  x=json.loads(f.read_text());y=json.loads((Path('agent/results')/base/f.name).read_text());assert x['num_prompts']==y['num_prompts']\n  rows.append(dict(asset=asset,end=end,n=x['num_prompts'],new=x['mean_crps'],base=y['mean_crps'],pct=100*(x['mean_crps']/y['mean_crps']-1)))\nd=pd.DataFrame(rows);d.to_csv('agent/results/width_temporal_audit.csv',index=False)\nprint(d.groupby('end').agg(new=('new','mean'),base=('base','mean'),pct=('pct','mean'),wins=('pct',lambda x:int((x<0).sum()))).to_string())\nnew=float((d.new*d.n).sum()/d.n.sum());base=float((d.base*d.n).sum()/d.n.sum())\nprint('Pooled official prompt means:',new,base,'pct',100*(new/base-1),'prompts',int(d.n.sum()))\nprint('Duration-weighted mean cell percentage:',float((d.pct*d.n).sum()/d.n.sum()))\nPY\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration66 width audit is mixed:scale1 versus0.95 regresses July0.1646% but improves August0.3154%. Thus0.95 has a material old high-volatility counterexample and is not universally calibrated. The audit compares the fixed choice with all three larger recent periods; pooled paired results are recorded in width_temporal_audit.csv. This audit was registered as temporal sensitivity/material-reversal review, not the strict all-historical-window veto used for new adaptive/covariance models. Do not conflate those standards or hide the counterexample.\n\n## Iteration67 — independent-seed width audit\n\nHypothesis: the selected crypto24h0.95 width gain survives Monte Carlo fan variation. Run v9 crypto24h at scales1 and0.95 on both full windows under seeds11 and37,1000 paths,float32. Require favorable means in all four seed/window comparisons and most cells. No new width values are allowed. This directly checks the possibility that narrowing mainly compensates one fixed random fan's dispersion, raised by the sampler experiments and historical reversal. Four CPU workers use the allocation released by the completed width-history audit.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\njobs=[]\nfor seed in [11,37]:\n for label,scale in [('control',1.),('narrow',.95)]:\n  tag=f'width_seed{seed}_{label}'\n  jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v9_research','--config',json.dumps({'scale':scale}),'--seed',str(seed),'--cached-prompts','--prediction-dtype','float32','--days','10','--ends','2026-09-19','2026-10-11','--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','24h','--workers','4'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_width_seeds.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_width_seeds.json > agent/results/queue_width_seeds.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"                    new         base       pct  wins\nend                                                 \n2026-07-22  3365.725070  3372.638976 -0.163411     3\n2026-08-22  9025.510616  8996.240834  0.316963     1\n2026-09-19  4201.615494  4210.541374 -0.219114     5\n2026-10-01  4269.655638  4289.144191 -0.481181     5\n2026-10-11  3406.152181  3424.434024 -0.540829     5\nPooled official prompt means: 4219.2935382365895 4231.270847531259 pct -0.2830664763910806 prompts 3840\nDuration-weighted mean cell percentage: -0.34818058623357045\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
