{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_421","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration56 corrected cache gate PASSED: exact uncached-versus-disk forecast equality, reload without inference, and changed-seed cache miss. The sequential recovery queue is now running; the original metadata failure remains archived.\n\nIteration65 result: price-mean correction worsens both COM means (+0.0068%/+0.0067%) and reverses sign for crypto24h (+0.0104%/-0.0158%) and1h (+0.0060%/-0.0034%). DISCARD all groups. The mathematical centering convention does not improve this empirical objective consistently.\n\nIteration64 matched constant fails added September (+0.0027%) and new historical July (+0.0205%,0/5 wins), despite favorable full-window results. DISCARD. Historical August's per-asset percentage mean slightly improves while raw configuration CRPS worsens; report this distinction, not an unqualified win.\n\nIteration67 width seed audit PASSED: all20 additional-seed cells improve. Seed11 mean reductions0.2052%/0.5239%; seed37 0.2090%/0.5270%. Across the five disjoint default-seed windows,0.95 reduces pooled official CRPS4231.2708→4219.2935 over3840 prompts (0.2831%); duration-weighted mean cell gain0.3482%. KEEP the simple current width based on this broader loss reduction and independent-seed evidence, while explicitly retaining August's0.3170% counterexample. This is not a universal-calibration claim or a retroactive pass of the stricter adaptive-model veto.\n\n## Iteration68 — relax narrowing only in hot24h states\n\nHypothesis: the historical width counterexample reflects hot regimes where the long-memory variance forecast lags. For crypto24h only, smoothly relax the selected0.95 width toward1 when initial/long variance rises from1 to2, and decay that relaxation with the existing forward-variance half-life. Formula:scale(t)=0.95+0.05*clip(log(initial/long)/log(2),0,1)*decay(t). Do not tune the threshold, endpoints or half-life.\n\nTest this single state-based policy against v9 on both full windows, added September, the old causal historical windows and the new historical date pair (with matched new24h controls). Require favorable full-window and added-period means and historical agreement before selecting it; otherwise keep the fixed width with its documented limitation. No new scalar-width grid. Four workers are released by completed seed tests.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('agent/research_model.py');s=p.read_text();needle=\\\"    sig=np.sqrt(np.maximum(variance,1e-14))*scale\\\";assert needle in s;s=s.replace(needle,\\\"    if c.get('heat_scale',False) and not short and asset in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE']:\\\\n        heat=np.clip(np.log(max(initial,1e-14)/max(long,1e-14))/np.log(2.),0.,1.)\\\\n        scale=scale+(1-scale)*heat*decay\\\\n\\\"+needle);p.write_text(s)\nhist={'table':'seasonality_jul01.json','clock_table':'clock_jul01.json','event_table':'event_multipliers_jul01.json'}\nspecs=[('heat_scale_v9_full',{'heat_scale':True},10,['2026-09-19','2026-10-11']),('sep_late_heat_scale',{'heat_scale':True},8,['2026-10-01']),('historical_heat_scale',{**hist,'heat_scale':True},2,['2026-07-22','2026-08-22']),('historical_new_v9_crypto24h',hist,2,['2026-07-29','2026-08-29']),('historical_new_heat_scale',{**hist,'heat_scale':True},2,['2026-07-29','2026-08-29'])]\njobs=[]\nfor tag,cfg,days,ends in specs:\n jobs.append({'cmd':['uv','run','agent/run_suite.py','--tag',tag,'--model','candidate_v9_research','--config',json.dumps(cfg),'--cached-prompts','--prediction-dtype','float32','--days',str(days),'--ends',*ends,'--assets','BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','--formats','24h','--workers','4'],'log':f'agent/results/{tag}_suite.log'})\nPath('agent/queue_heat_scale.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_heat_scale.json > agent/results/queue_heat_scale.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_422","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration69 — shorten learned decoding only if exactly equivalent\n\nThe selected learned horizon is one hour, yet the helper decodes25 hourly values inherited from the rejected24h experiment. At ordinary issuance boundaries, three hourly predictions cover the full requested hour. Test whether seeded three-step Chronos decoding exactly reproduces the first three values/samples of25-step decoding on real BTC/HYPE contexts, including an hour-boundary case. If any prefix or averaged forecast differs, do not treat this as a transparent speed optimization. No CRPS is measured here.\n\nRun as oneGPU process only after the complete recovery queue PID67090 exits, so cache-populating and cached comparisons are unaffected. Record inference times separately from the existing serving benchmarks. Do not change forecasting code or invalidate caches before the current studies finish.\nEOF\ncat > agent/verify_chronos_prefix.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Verify short decoding preserves the seeded forecast prefix exactly.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport os,random,time,json\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd,torch\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import default_store_root\nfrom predict import load_minute_prices,context_end\nfrom research_model import shape_at\nfrom chronos_vol import pipeline\nseed=int(os.environ.get('SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED','20261011'))\nmodel=pipeline();rows=[]\nfor asset,date in [('BTC','2026-09-16T00:02:00Z'),('HYPE','2026-10-08T13:17:00Z')]:\n t=pd.Timestamp(date);frame=load_minute_prices(default_store_root(asset).parents[2],asset,t-pd.Timedelta(days=8),t)\n end=context_end(t,3600);frame=frame.loc[(frame.index>end-pd.Timedelta(days=7))&(frame.index<=end)]\n ret=np.log(frame.close.astype(float)).diff();rv=ret.pow(2)/shape_at(frame.index,asset,True)\n hourly=rv.resample('h').mean();count=frame.close.resample('h').size()\n hourly=hourly[(count==60)&(hourly.index+pd.Timedelta(hours=1)<=frame.index[-1]+pd.Timedelta(minutes=1))].iloc[-144:]\n values=hourly.to_numpy();center=float(np.nanmedian(values));series=np.log(np.maximum(values,center*.001)/center)\n forecasts={};elapsed={}\n for length in [25,3]:\n  random.seed(seed);torch.manual_seed(seed)\n  if torch.cuda.is_available():torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n  started=time.perf_counter()\n  with torch.inference_mode():pred=model.predict(torch.tensor(series,dtype=torch.float32),prediction_length=length,num_samples=32)\n  forecasts[length]=pred.detach().cpu().numpy()[0];elapsed[length]=time.perf_counter()-started\n mean25=np.mean(np.exp(np.clip(forecasts[25],-3,3)),axis=0)*center\n mean3=np.mean(np.exp(np.clip(forecasts[3],-3,3)),axis=0)*center\n origin=hourly.index[-1]+pd.Timedelta(hours=1)\n max_index=int((t+pd.Timedelta(hours=1)-origin).total_seconds()//3600)\n row={'asset':asset,'start_time':str(t),'sample_prefix_equal':bool(np.array_equal(forecasts[25][:,:3],forecasts[3])),'mean_prefix_equal':bool(np.array_equal(mean25[:3],mean3)),'max_mean_difference':float(np.max(np.abs(mean25[:3]-mean3))),'required_forecast_values':max_index+1,'seconds':elapsed}\n rows.append(row);print(json.dumps(row),flush=True)\nassert all(r['sample_prefix_equal'] and r['mean_prefix_equal'] and r['required_forecast_values']<=3 for r in rows)\nPY\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nPath('agent/queue_chronos_prefix.json').write_text(json.dumps([{'cmd':['uv','run','--group','research','agent/verify_chronos_prefix.py'],'log':'agent/results/chronos_prefix_parity.log'}],indent=2))\nPY\nuv run agent/queue_research.py --jobs agent/queue_chronos_prefix.json --after-pid 67090 > agent/results/queue_chronos_prefix.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
